IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cca-patron`
IMPORT `cca-qa`

-- Casino Control Act 1984 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (cca-qa.l4): every exported question, for every role and
-- every situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for the two roles it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the
-- answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation with an error. Each
-- question with a situation input is asked, for its own role, with the situation FALSE and every later input ASSUMEd.
-- For the patron (the baseline's seat), each question is also asked against the baseline export on the same facts.
-- Mirror cases ask the same facts from the patron and the employee (removal), and from the child and the parent (s 27(4),
-- s 27(3a)). Expected values are worked by hand from the deposited text, never copied from the output. The people are
-- HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked person` IS A `Who wants me kept out`
ASSUME `an unasked who` IS A `Who banned me`
ASSUME `an unasked offence` IS A `Patron offence`
ASSUME `an unasked reason` IS A `Why there, and with whom`
ASSUME `an unasked game` IS A `Kind of game`

`as the patron` MEANS `I go, or want to go, to a casino in Western Australia`
`as the employee` MEANS `I work at a casino in Western Australia, as a casino employee or key employee`
`as the parent` MEANS `I want to take a child under 18 into a casino with me`

GIVEN `who` IS A `Who banned me`, `hours` IS A NUMBER, `revoked` IS A BOOLEAN, `revoked on review` IS A BOOLEAN
      `casino told of it` IS A BOOLEAN, `casino told of revocation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `My ban`
`a ban by` MEANS `My ban` WITH
    `who banned me` IS `who`
    `hours since the ban was made` IS `hours`
    `the person who made it has revoked it` IS `revoked`
    `the Commission has revoked it on review and given notice` IS `revoked on review`
    `the casino has been given written notice of the ban` IS `casino told of it`
    `the casino has been given written notice of the revocation` IS `casino told of revocation`

`not banned` MEANS `a ban by` `nobody` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`banned on the spot 10 hours ago` MEANS `a ban by` `the casino on the spot` 10 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`banned on the spot 25 hours ago` MEANS `a ban by` `the casino on the spot` 25 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`banned by casino direction` MEANS `a ban by` `the casino by written direction` 100 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`casino direction revoked on review` MEANS `a ban by` `the casino by written direction` 100 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`banned by police, casino told` MEANS `a ban by` `the Commissioner of Police by written direction` 100 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`banned by police, casino not told` MEANS `a ban by` `the Commissioner of Police by written direction` 100 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER, `why` IS A `Why I am there`, `accompanied` IS A BOOLEAN, `plays` IS A BOOLEAN, `game` IS A `Kind of game`
GIVETH A `My visit`
`a visit at` MEANS `My visit` WITH
    `my age in years` IS `age`
    `why I am there` IS `why`
    `with my spouse, parent or guardian who is over 18` IS `accompanied`
    `I play` IS `plays`
    `the game` IS `game`
    `it is played to the approved rules` IS TRUE

`an adult playing blackjack` MEANS `a visit at` 30 `to gamble or for anything else` FALSE TRUE `an authorised game`
`an adult at a poker machine` MEANS `a visit at` 30 `to gamble or for anything else` FALSE TRUE `a game played with a poker machine`
`an adult not playing` MEANS `a visit at` 30 `to gamble or for anything else` FALSE FALSE `no game`
`a 15-year-old at dinner with a parent` MEANS `a visit at` 15 `to have a meal` TRUE FALSE `no game`
`a 15-year-old at dinner alone` MEANS `a visit at` 15 `to have a meal` FALSE FALSE `no game`
`a 15-year-old playing` MEANS `a visit at` 15 `to gamble or for anything else` FALSE TRUE `an authorised game`
`a 16-year-old looking around` MEANS `a visit at` 16 `to gamble or for anything else` FALSE FALSE `no game`

GIVEN `suspected` IS A BOOLEAN, `appeared false` IS A BOOLEAN, `evidence` IS A BOOLEAN, `left` IS A BOOLEAN, `excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Age check`
`an age check` MEANS `Age check` WITH
    `an authorised person suspected on reasonable grounds that I am under 18` IS `suspected`
    `my stated age appeared false to them` IS `appeared false`
    `I produced evidence of my age` IS `evidence`
    `I left when required` IS `left`
    `I had a reasonable excuse for not leaving` IS `excuse`

`no age check` MEANS `an age check` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`no proof, stayed` MEANS `an age check` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`no proof, left` MEANS `an age check` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`no proof, stayed with an excuse` MEANS `an age check` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE

§§ `For the casino patron`

-- s 26: the casino may ban on the spot or by direction; my family has no power; the Commission only reviews.
#ASSERT `Who can keep me out of the casino and how` `as the patron` `the casino` EQUALS `ban you on the spot for up to 24 hours (s 26(1a)), or by written direction until the casino revokes it (s 26(2))`
#ASSERT `Who can keep me out of the casino and how` `as the patron` `a member of my family` EQUALS `nothing: the Act gives your family no power to ban you and no right to apply for a ban`
#ASSERT `Who can keep me out of the casino and how` `as the patron` `the Gaming and Wagering Commission` EQUALS `not ban you, but confirm or revoke a casino direction if you apply for review (s 26A)`
#ASSERT `Who can keep me out of the casino and how` `as the patron` `I myself` EQUALS `the keeping-out answer for` (`What can this person do to keep me out of the casino` `I myself`)
#ASSERT `May a member of my family apply to have me banned` `as the patron` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May a member of my family apply to have me banned` `as the patron` EQUALS `yes if` `May my family apply to have me banned`
#ASSERT `Have I a right to enter or stay in the casino against its wishes` `as the patron` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Have I a right to enter or stay in the casino against its wishes` `as the patron` EQUALS `yes if` `Have I a right to enter the casino`
-- s 26(1b), (3), (4): an on-the-spot ban 10 hours old is in force, 25 hours old is not; a police direction once the
-- casino is told; a casino direction revoked on review is not.
#ASSERT `Is the ban on me in force now` `as the patron` TRUE `the casino on the spot` 10 FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is the ban on me in force now` `as the patron` TRUE `the casino on the spot` 25 FALSE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is the ban on me in force now` `as the patron` TRUE `the Commissioner of Police by written direction` 100 FALSE TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is the ban on me in force now` `as the patron` TRUE `the Commissioner of Police by written direction` 100 FALSE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is the ban on me in force now` `as the patron` TRUE `the casino by written direction` 100 TRUE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is the ban on me in force now` `as the patron` TRUE `the casino by written direction` 100 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`Is the ban on me in force` `banned by casino direction`)
-- s 26A(1): only a casino's written direction is reviewable; r 4: $179; s 26A(2): it stays in force meanwhile.
#ASSERT `May I apply for a review of the ban on me` `as the patron` TRUE `the casino by written direction` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May I apply for a review of the ban on me` `as the patron` TRUE `the casino on the spot` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May I apply for a review of the ban on me` `as the patron` TRUE `the Commissioner of Police by written direction` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May I apply for a review of the ban on me` `as the patron` TRUE `the Commissioner of Police by written direction` EQUALS `yes if` (`May I apply to have my ban reviewed` `banned by police, casino told`)
#ASSERT `What fee must I pay for a review of the ban` `as the patron` TRUE EQUALS amount 179
#ASSERT `What fee must I pay for a review of the ban` `as the patron` TRUE EQUALS amount `What fee must I pay for a review`
#ASSERT `Does the ban on me stay in force during the review` `as the patron` TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Does the ban on me stay in force during the review` `as the patron` TRUE EQUALS `yes if` `Does my ban stay in force during the review`
-- The court maxima: $50 000 for playing while banned; $1 000 first and $2 000 later for a child entering; $5 000 under an
-- on-the-spot ban. The infringement amounts: $1 000 under a direction; $200 for a child gaming.
#ASSERT `What is the most a court can fine me for this casino offence` `as the patron` `playing while banned (s 23(2)(ii))` `an unasked fact` EQUALS amount 50000
#ASSERT `What is the most a court can fine me for this casino offence` `as the patron` `entering or staying under 18 (s 27(3))` FALSE EQUALS amount 1000
#ASSERT `What is the most a court can fine me for this casino offence` `as the patron` `entering or staying under 18 (s 27(3))` TRUE EQUALS amount 2000
#ASSERT `What is the most a court can fine me for this casino offence` `as the patron` `entering or staying under an on-the-spot ban (s 26(1d))` `an unasked fact` EQUALS amount 5000
#ASSERT `What is the most a court can fine me for this casino offence` `as the patron` `entering or staying under 18 (s 27(3))` TRUE EQUALS amount (`What is the most I can be fined for` `entering or staying under 18 (s 27(3))` TRUE)
#ASSERT `What would an infringement notice ask me to pay for this offence` `as the patron` `entering or staying under a written direction (s 26(6))` EQUALS amount 1000
#ASSERT `What would an infringement notice ask me to pay for this offence` `as the patron` `gaming under 18 (s 27(3a))` EQUALS amount 200
#ASSERT `What would an infringement notice ask me to pay for this offence` `as the patron` `gaming under 18 (s 27(3a))` EQUALS amount (`What would an infringement notice ask me to pay` `gaming under 18 (s 27(3a))`)
-- ss 23(2b), 27(3b): forfeiture on the prosecutor's application, for playing while banned or gaming under 18 only.
#ASSERT `Must the court take my winnings` `as the patron` TRUE `playing while banned (s 23(2)(ii))` TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Must the court take my winnings` `as the patron` TRUE `entering or staying under a written direction (s 26(6))` TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Must the court take my winnings` `as the patron` TRUE `playing while banned (s 23(2)(ii))` FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Must the court take my winnings` `as the patron` TRUE `gaming under 18 (s 27(3a))` TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`Must my winnings be forfeited` `gaming under 18 (s 27(3a))` TRUE)
-- s 27(4): a 15-year-old at dinner with a parent, not playing: yes; alone: no; playing: no; an adult: no (not under 18).
#ASSERT `Does s 27(4) let me into the casino although I am under 18` `as the patron` 15 `to have a meal, with a spouse, parent or guardian over 18 (or a person over 18 in place of a parent)` FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Does s 27(4) let me into the casino although I am under 18` `as the patron` 15 `to have a meal, without one` FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Does s 27(4) let me into the casino although I am under 18` `as the patron` 15 `to gamble, or for anything else` TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Does s 27(4) let me into the casino although I am under 18` `as the patron` 30 `to gamble, or for anything else` FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Does s 27(4) let me into the casino although I am under 18` `as the patron` 15 `to have a meal, without one` FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`Does s 27(4) let me in although I am under 18` `a 15-year-old at dinner alone`)
-- ss 26(6), 27(3): a 16-year-old looking around: yes; an adult not banned: no; an adult under a casino direction: yes;
-- the 15-year-old at dinner with a parent: no.
#ASSERT `Is it an offence for me to enter or stay in the casino` `as the patron` `nobody` 0 FALSE FALSE 16 `to gamble, or for anything else` FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is it an offence for me to enter or stay in the casino` `as the patron` `nobody` 0 FALSE FALSE 30 `to gamble, or for anything else` FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is it an offence for me to enter or stay in the casino` `as the patron` `the casino by written direction` 100 FALSE FALSE 30 `to gamble, or for anything else` FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is it an offence for me to enter or stay in the casino` `as the patron` `nobody` 0 FALSE FALSE 15 `to have a meal, with a spouse, parent or guardian over 18 (or a person over 18 in place of a parent)` FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is it an offence for me to enter or stay in the casino` `as the patron` `the casino by written direction` 100 FALSE FALSE 30 `to gamble, or for anything else` FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`Is it an offence for me to enter or stay` `banned by casino direction` `an adult not playing`)
-- ss 23(2)(ii), 27(3a): banned and playing: yes; an adult not banned playing: no; a child playing: yes.
#ASSERT `Is it an offence for me to play in the casino` `as the patron` `the casino by written direction` 100 FALSE FALSE 30 TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is it an offence for me to play in the casino` `as the patron` `nobody` 0 FALSE FALSE 30 TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is it an offence for me to play in the casino` `as the patron` `nobody` 0 FALSE FALSE 15 TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is it an offence for me to play in the casino` `as the patron` `nobody` 0 FALSE FALSE 15 TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`Is it an offence for me to play` `not banned` `a 15-year-old playing`)
-- The largest single maximum: banned and playing $50 000; an on-the-spot ban $5 000; a direction $10 000; a child playing
-- $2 000; a child looking around $1 000, or $2 000 after an earlier conviction; an adult not banned $0.
#ASSERT `What is the largest fine I risk for this visit to the casino` `as the patron` `the casino by written direction` 100 FALSE FALSE 30 `to gamble, or for anything else` TRUE FALSE EQUALS amount 50000
#ASSERT `What is the largest fine I risk for this visit to the casino` `as the patron` `the casino on the spot` 10 FALSE FALSE 30 `to gamble, or for anything else` FALSE FALSE EQUALS amount 5000
#ASSERT `What is the largest fine I risk for this visit to the casino` `as the patron` `the casino by written direction` 100 FALSE FALSE 30 `to gamble, or for anything else` FALSE FALSE EQUALS amount 10000
#ASSERT `What is the largest fine I risk for this visit to the casino` `as the patron` `nobody` 0 FALSE FALSE 15 `to gamble, or for anything else` TRUE FALSE EQUALS amount 2000
#ASSERT `What is the largest fine I risk for this visit to the casino` `as the patron` `nobody` 0 FALSE FALSE 16 `to gamble, or for anything else` FALSE FALSE EQUALS amount 1000
#ASSERT `What is the largest fine I risk for this visit to the casino` `as the patron` `nobody` 0 FALSE FALSE 16 `to gamble, or for anything else` FALSE TRUE EQUALS amount 2000
#ASSERT `What is the largest fine I risk for this visit to the casino` `as the patron` `nobody` 0 FALSE FALSE 30 `to gamble, or for anything else` TRUE FALSE EQUALS amount 0
#ASSERT `What is the largest fine I risk for this visit to the casino` `as the patron` `nobody` 0 FALSE FALSE 16 `to gamble, or for anything else` FALSE TRUE EQUALS amount (`What is the largest fine I risk for this visit` `not banned` `a 16-year-old looking around` TRUE)
-- ss 22(1), 23(1)(b): an authorised game to the approved rules: yes; a poker machine: no.
#ASSERT `Is the game I am playing lawful in the casino` `as the patron` `an authorised game` TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is the game I am playing lawful in the casino` `as the patron` `a game played with a poker machine` TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is the game I am playing lawful in the casino` `as the patron` `a game played with a poker machine` TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`Is the game lawful in the casino` `an adult at a poker machine`)
-- ss 26(1c), (5), 27A(3): banned: yes; a 16-year-old who could not prove their age and stayed: yes; who left: no.
#ASSERT `May I be removed from the casino with reasonable force` `as the patron` `the casino by written direction` 100 FALSE FALSE 30 `to gamble, or for anything else` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May I be removed from the casino with reasonable force` `as the patron` `nobody` 0 FALSE FALSE 16 `to gamble, or for anything else` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May I be removed from the casino with reasonable force` `as the patron` `nobody` 0 FALSE FALSE 16 `to gamble, or for anything else` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May I be removed from the casino with reasonable force` `as the patron` `nobody` 0 FALSE FALSE 16 `to gamble, or for anything else` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`May I be removed with reasonable force` `not banned` `a 16-year-old looking around` `no proof, left`)
-- s 27A(4)(b): stayed without proof and without excuse: yes; with a reasonable excuse: no.
#ASSERT `Have I committed the offence of not leaving the casino` `as the patron` 16 `to gamble, or for anything else` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Have I committed the offence of not leaving the casino` `as the patron` 16 `to gamble, or for anything else` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Have I committed the offence of not leaving the casino` `as the patron` 16 `to gamble, or for anything else` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`Have I committed the offence of not leaving` `a 16-year-old looking around` `no proof, stayed with an excuse`)

-- Added after verification (6 November 2026; Q9 in NOTES.md): the layer asks the facts of a ban, a visit and an age
-- check as separate inputs, with some folded together. Each case asks the layer on the folded inputs and asserts the
-- baseline's answer on a record that sets the facts the other way the folding allows.
-- A casino direction the Commission revoked on review (s 26A(5)(b)) is given to the layer as revoked: not in force.
#ASSERT `Is the ban on me in force now` `as the patron` TRUE `the casino by written direction` 100 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`Is the ban on me in force` `casino direction revoked on review`)
-- A police direction revoked, but the casino not told of the revocation (s 26(4)(b)), is not yet revoked: in force.
#ASSERT `Is the ban on me in force now` `as the patron` TRUE `the Commissioner of Police by written direction` 100 FALSE TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is the ban on me in force now` `as the patron` TRUE `the Commissioner of Police by written direction` 100 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`Is the ban on me in force` (`a ban by` `the Commissioner of Police by written direction` 100 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE))
-- A police direction revoked with written notice to the casino: not in force.
#ASSERT `Is the ban on me in force now` `as the patron` TRUE `the Commissioner of Police by written direction` 100 TRUE TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is the ban on me in force now` `as the patron` TRUE `the Commissioner of Police by written direction` 100 TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`Is the ban on me in force` (`a ban by` `the Commissioner of Police by written direction` 100 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE))
-- An on-the-spot ban revoked within the 24 hours: not in force.
#ASSERT `Is the ban on me in force now` `as the patron` TRUE `the casino on the spot` 2 TRUE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is the ban on me in force now` `as the patron` TRUE `the casino on the spot` 2 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`Is the ban on me in force` (`a ban by` `the casino on the spot` 2 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- s 27(4)(a): a 16-year-old working in the amenities, not playing: let in, whether or not a parent is with them.
#ASSERT `Does s 27(4) let me into the casino although I am under 18` `as the patron` 16 `to work in the amenities ancillary to the gaming` FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Does s 27(4) let me into the casino although I am under 18` `as the patron` 16 `to work in the amenities ancillary to the gaming` FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`Does s 27(4) let me in although I am under 18` (`a visit at` 16 `to work in the amenities ancillary to the gaming` TRUE FALSE `no game`))
-- s 27(4)(b): a meal with a parent but playing: not let in; an offence to enter (s 27(3)) and to play (s 27(3a)).
#ASSERT `Is it an offence for me to enter or stay in the casino` `as the patron` `nobody` 0 FALSE FALSE 15 `to have a meal, with a spouse, parent or guardian over 18 (or a person over 18 in place of a parent)` TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is it an offence for me to enter or stay in the casino` `as the patron` `nobody` 0 FALSE FALSE 15 `to have a meal, with a spouse, parent or guardian over 18 (or a person over 18 in place of a parent)` TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`Is it an offence for me to enter or stay` `not banned` (`a visit at` 15 `to have a meal` TRUE TRUE `a game played with a poker machine`))
-- s 27A(3): suspected and asked, but the stated age did not appear false: no requirement to leave, so no removal on that
-- ground; the layer's one input is FALSE.
#ASSERT `May I be removed from the casino with reasonable force` `as the patron` `nobody` 0 FALSE FALSE 16 `to gamble, or for anything else` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May I be removed from the casino with reasonable force` `as the patron` `nobody` 0 FALSE FALSE 16 `to gamble, or for anything else` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`May I be removed with reasonable force` `not banned` `a 16-year-old looking around` (`an age check` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- ... and one who produced evidence of age: no offence of not leaving (s 27A(4)(b)).
#ASSERT `Have I committed the offence of not leaving the casino` `as the patron` 16 `to gamble, or for anything else` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Have I committed the offence of not leaving the casino` `as the patron` 16 `to gamble, or for anything else` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`Have I committed the offence of not leaving` `a 16-year-old looking around` (`an age check` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
-- A police direction the casino has been told of, removal by an authorised employee: the patron's and the employee's
-- seats agree (s 26(5)).
#ASSERT `May I be removed from the casino with reasonable force` `as the patron` `the Commissioner of Police by written direction` 100 FALSE TRUE 30 `to gamble, or for anything else` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May I remove this person from the casino with reasonable force` `as the employee` TRUE `the Commissioner of Police by written direction` 100 FALSE TRUE 30 `to gamble, or for anything else` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May I remove this person from the casino with reasonable force` `as the employee` TRUE `the Commissioner of Police by written direction` 100 FALSE FALSE 30 `to gamble, or for anything else` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS no

§§ `For the casino employee`

-- s 23(2)(ia), (2a): only where required to play for a duty; $50 000; forfeiture on application (s 23(2b)).
#ASSERT `May I play a game in the casino where I work` `as the employee` TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May I play a game in the casino where I work` `as the employee` FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for playing in the casino where I work` `as the employee` EQUALS amount 50000
#ASSERT `Must the court take my winnings from playing where I work` `as the employee` TRUE TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Must the court take my winnings from playing where I work` `as the employee` TRUE FALSE EQUALS no
-- s 26(1a), (1b): an authorised person may prohibit on the spot, for up to 24 hours.
#ASSERT `May I prohibit this person from the casino on the spot` `as the employee` TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `How long does my on-the-spot prohibition last at most` `as the employee` TRUE EQUALS `up to` 24
-- s 27A(1): on reasonable suspicion, not of a child let in by s 27(4).
#ASSERT `May I require this person to state their age` `as the employee` TRUE TRUE 16 `to gamble, or for anything else` FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May I require this person to state their age` `as the employee` TRUE TRUE 15 `to have a meal, with a spouse, parent or guardian over 18 (or a person over 18 in place of a parent)` FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May I require this person to state their age` `as the employee` TRUE FALSE `an unasked number` `an unasked reason` `an unasked fact` EQUALS no
-- Mirror of the patron's removal cases: same facts, same answers.
#ASSERT `May I remove this person from the casino with reasonable force` `as the employee` TRUE `the casino by written direction` 100 FALSE FALSE 30 `to gamble, or for anything else` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May I remove this person from the casino with reasonable force` `as the employee` TRUE `nobody` 0 FALSE FALSE 16 `to gamble, or for anything else` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May I remove this person from the casino with reasonable force` `as the employee` TRUE `nobody` 0 FALSE FALSE 16 `to gamble, or for anything else` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS no
-- s 27(1), (1a), (2): a 15-year-old playing, no reasonable belief: yes; with it: no; at dinner with a parent: no; an
-- adult: no. $50 000 if they played, $20 000 if not.
#ASSERT `Have I committed an offence by letting a person under 18 in` `as the employee` TRUE 15 `to gamble, or for anything else` TRUE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Have I committed an offence by letting a person under 18 in` `as the employee` TRUE 15 `to gamble, or for anything else` TRUE TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Have I committed an offence by letting a person under 18 in` `as the employee` TRUE 15 `to have a meal, with a spouse, parent or guardian over 18 (or a person over 18 in place of a parent)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Have I committed an offence by letting a person under 18 in` `as the employee` TRUE 30 `to gamble, or for anything else` TRUE `an unasked fact` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for a person under 18 being let in` `as the employee` TRUE TRUE EQUALS amount 50000
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for a person under 18 being let in` `as the employee` TRUE FALSE EQUALS amount 20000

§§ `For the parent, spouse or guardian`

-- Mirror of the child's s 27(4) cases: 15, with a parent, for a meal, not playing: yes; without the parent: no; not only
-- for a meal: no; playing: no.
#ASSERT `May the child come into the casino with me for a meal` `as the parent` 15 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May the child come into the casino with me for a meal` `as the parent` 15 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May the child come into the casino with me for a meal` `as the parent` 15 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May the child come into the casino with me for a meal` `as the parent` 15 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS no
-- Mirror of the child playing (s 27(3a)): 15, yes.
#ASSERT `Would the child commit an offence by playing` `as the parent` 15 EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Would the child commit an offence by playing` `as the parent` 17 EQUALS yes

§§ `Does not arise`

-- Each question for the roles it is not about: every other input ASSUMEd.
#ASSERT `Who can keep me out of the casino and how` `as the employee` `an unasked person` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Who can keep me out of the casino and how` `as the parent` `an unasked person` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `May a member of my family apply to have me banned` `as the employee` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `May a member of my family apply to have me banned` `as the parent` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Have I a right to enter or stay in the casino against its wishes` `as the employee` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
